& [SupportDelta] remains before M2C
  + the topology-scanner formation RacePolicy still says strength is quiescent_double_inventory
  + its ReceiptContract still names consistency and assigns quiescent_double_inventory
  + its formation trace predates topology receipt 0.3 and the replacement signatures
  + its future whole-root repetition does not yet bind two distinct actual acquisition identities, their exact order, complete independent lineages, common scope, both canonical digests, and the pure reconciliation result
  + therefore the formation graph is historically preserved but not current implementation authority

& [BoundaryDiagnosis] is authority lineage drift
  + [not_a_runtime_fault] no topology scanner, receipt issuer, receipt ledger, or M2C consumer exists
  + [not_a_forms_fault] current machine and receipt forms reject the legacy representation exactly
  + [not_permission_to_edit_history] preserved source and canonical formation remain immutable evidence of the prior decision
  + [repair_need] one derived revision source must supersede only the stale formation meaning before any M2C source can be selected

& [CandidateComparison] is dependency ordered
  + [candidate_A] proceed directly to M2C scanner implementation
    - rejected because formation grants no implementation or execution authority and its receipt meaning is stale
  + [candidate_B] interpret the completed child form revision as silently rewriting the parent formation
    - rejected because implicit transitive mutation destroys inspectable authority and signature meaning
  + [candidate_C] edit the preserved scanner source or canonical formation in place
    - rejected because SourceSpecificationPreservation requires immutable prior input and explicit supersession
  + [candidate_D] create physical acquisition, traversal, or receipt-issuer code to discover the desired contract
    - rejected because code cannot be the source of governing meaning and physical authority remains locked
  + [candidate_E] revise the entire scanner protocol, platform surface, or profile now
    - rejected because no evidence requires behavior, API, platform, or scanner-profile change
  + [candidate_F] source-preserve one formation-only consistency-evidence reconciliation
    + supersede legacy evidence vocabulary and receipt field references
    + retain scanner profile cantor-windows-candidate-topology/0.1
    + bind future non-atomic evidence to two distinct complete actual acquisitions, exact first-then-second order, identical declared scope, both canonical digest lineages, and current pure Equal reconciliation
    + distinguish pure receipt-form validity from scanner issuance
    + retain every original no-follow, traversal, Git, limit, fault, platform-seam, and staged-authority prohibition unless the SJS audit finds a contradiction
    + grant no code, Win32, filesystem, fixture, receipt issuance, consumption, mutation, or effect authority

& [SelectedBoundary] is topology scanner formation consistency-evidence reconciliation
  + [profile_candidate] is cantor-phase3-topology-scanner-formation-consistency-evidence-reconciliation/0.1
  + [artifact_class] is source-preserved canonical formation revision and replacement formation signature only
  + [scanner_profile] remains cantor-windows-candidate-topology/0.1
